HALF_UP` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` and update the import to match.\n\n**CI:** passed (run ci-0001, sha 08d3cd5986).", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 379737, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01DUh78NQr1epPhRwpxBsGyP", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 379737, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DUh78NQr1epPhRwpxBsGyP", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 383785, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** In `src/money.py`, `round_money` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). So `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of the `2.66` the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On the new branch `fix/money-bankers-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` and updated the import. That one line is the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n\nFIN-212 doesn't exist as a security advisory. It's probably an internal ticket, so I relied on the docstring and the test for the intended behaviour. I haven't merged the PR; merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Let me look at the relevant files first.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01NS3PH1wTG9cv35ohM4fw9p", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}